# The edge in front of the app (link addresses spec 2026-11-18 §5.6): HTTPS for the platform's own host and for every
# brand's link address, with certificates fetched on the first request and renewed by Caddy.
#
# - Before Caddy asks for a certificate it calls the app's host-allowed endpoint; only a host the app knows (the
#   platform's, a brand's current one, or a former one still within the pages' 90 days) gets one. A stranger pointing
#   a name at this server gets none.
# - Caddy must be the only thing listening on 443 (and on 80, for the certificate challenge).
# - Caddy keeps the original Host header when it proxies, so the app needs no omnichannel.pages.trust-forwarded-host.
# - The app's port here is 8080; change both lines if it runs elsewhere.
{
	on_demand_tls {
		ask http://localhost:8080/internal/pages/host-allowed
	}
}

https:// {
	tls {
		on_demand
	}
	reverse_proxy localhost:8080
}
